    docs(npm12): verify the allowScripts remedy on a real npm 12.2.2 and align script/README/probe (DF-SPECLANG-019)
    
    Printed today (postinstall-lint-deps.sh npm>=12 branch + README troubleshooting):
      1. "allowScripts": { "better-sqlite3": true }
         or npm install-scripts approve --no-allow-scripts-pin better-sqlite3
      2. npm rebuild better-sqlite3
      3. npm run check:sqlite-binding
    
    What actually happened, on npm 12.2.2 / node v22.22.3 / better-sqlite3 12.11.1, in a scratch
    project outside the repo with no .npmrc:
    
    - Reproduction: install with no allowScripts exits 0 and warns "1 package had install scripts
      blocked because they are not covered by allowScripts: better-sqlite3@12.11.1 (install:
      prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release)"; require('better-sqlite3') then fails with
      "Could not locate the bindings file" and no build/ directory exists.
    - `npm install-scripts approve --no-allow-scripts-pin better-sqlite3` exits 0, prints
      "Approved better-sqlite3: / added better-sqlite3" and writes the unpinned allowScripts entry.
      It builds nothing: the binding is still missing immediately after it.
    - `npm rebuild better-sqlite3` exits 0 ("rebuilt dependencies successfully"), creates
      build/Release/better_sqlite3.node, and require + select sqlite_version() -> 3.53.2 succeeds;
      the repo gate prints OK: better-sqlite3 native binding loads (SELECT 1 -> {"x":1}).
    
    So the printed remedy is CORRECT as printed: no remedy command was changed.
    
    What was corrected/added, all grounded in that probe:
    - README: approve-then-rebuild order, plus the two traps measured here: `npm rebuild` exits 0
      while the install script is still blocked (judge the fix by check:sqlite-binding, never by its
      exit code), and an explicit "better-sqlite3": false deny entry makes `approve` a green no-op
      that has to be deleted by hand. Also records the pinned vs --no-allow-scripts-pin form and the
      verified versions.
    - scripts/postinstall-lint-deps.sh: a printed note carrying the same two traps and a verified
      line; the remedy steps themselves are byte-identical to before.
    - docs/npm12-allowscripts-probe.md: verbatim transcript (install warning, approve, rebuild,
      binding load) plus counter-probes: rebuild without approval (green no-op), deny blocking
      approve, default approve pinning the version, and a fresh install that already carries the
      approval.
    - tests/npm12-remedy-doc.test.ts: text-parity guard. Asserts the three remedy command strings
      appear in the script, README.md and the probe doc; that the approval JSON the script prints
      matches both the README and the real package.json allowScripts; and that README links the
      transcript. It never executes npm and runs in under a second.
    
    Note: the unattended harness blocks inline `node -e` payloads, so the binding probe in the
    transcript is a one-line file (check-binding.js) performing the same require + in-memory query.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
